  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "LuciferCore High-Performance Binary and Search Optimization Update\n\n      Architecture and Performance Overhaul\n      - Advanced Case-Insensitive Vectorization: Refactored FastBinary search routines to eliminate legacy slow-path scalar loops. Implemented localized bitwise ASCII normalization combined with native .NET 9 IndexOfAny SIMD intrinsics for single-byte lookups.\n      - High-Throughput Sub-Span Matching: Engineered a dedicated IndexOfSubSpanIgnoreCase pipeline featuring an accelerated SIMD Skip mechanism, bypassing mismatched data blocks at hardware bus speeds before falling back to unrolled byte-by-byte validation.\n      - Zero-Overhead Inline Primitives: Optimized char-path routing inside generic methods via low-level MemoryMarshal and Unsafe casting, entirely eliminating defensive memory copying and stack allocation penalties.\n      - API Consolidation: Permanently stripped away redundant Fill and Clear wrappers across FastBinary and Lucifer cores, encouraging direct native Span utilization to reduce codebase bloat and maximize JIT inline budgets.\n\n      Performance Results\n      - Single-Byte In-Memory Search: Case-insensitive byte search speeds surged by approximately 15 to 18 times on dense buffers, achieving parity with raw, non-normalized memory scans.\n      - Multi-Byte Sub-Span Evaluation: Large-scale case-insensitive pattern matching demonstrated a massive 9x to 20x latency reduction, slashing execution times on massive 268MB data arrays from 123ms down to just 14.8ms while maintaining a flawless Zero-Allocation footprint.",
